    12	    The function should return a tuple containing all planets whose orbits are 
    13	    located between the orbit of planet1 and the orbit of planet2, sorted by 
    14	    the proximity to the sun. 
    15	    The function should return an empty tuple if planet1 or planet2
    16	    are not correct planet names. 
    17	    Examples
    18	    bf("Jupiter", "Neptune") ==> ("Saturn", "Uranus")
    19	    bf("Earth", "Mercury") ==> ("Venus")
    20	    bf("Mercury", "Uranus") ==> ("Venus", "Earth", "Mars", "Jupiter", "Saturn")
    21	    '''
    22	    planet_names = ("Mercury", "Venus", "Earth", "Mars", "Jupiter", "Saturn", "Uranus", "Neptune")
    23	    if planet1 not in planet_names or planet2 not in planet_names or planet1 == planet2:
    24	        return ()
    25	    planet1_index = planet_names.index(planet1)
    26	    planet2_index = planet_names.index(planet2)
    27	    if planet1_index < planet2_index:
    28	        return (planet_names[planet1_index + 1: planet2_index])
    29	    else:
    30	        return (planet_names[planet2_index + 1 : planet1_index])
